\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{An equal-period square recovers rank 4}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{Take #{d=2}. \ref{fdip-00OQ} gives cohomology dimensions
#{1}, #{2} and #{1} over any field. For equal side lengths these
are the Betti numbers of \ref{fdip-008Z}. The counting operator
of \ref{fdip-00OL} therefore has kernel rank #{4} over an
ordered field, by \ref{fdip-00OP}. That is the kernel dimension
recorded for the counting adjoint in \ref{fdip-0090}.}
